# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the SHIP-3 gates (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/ship-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. Templates only: no tag is pushed from the
# branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the pass rule. ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-3 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed commit
# (sed -i 's/tp4-ship-3/<tag>/' *.env). The ship profile and its approved waiver are the ship pack's, byte for byte. Nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# B0 (STOP): build the SHIP-3 image from the pushed tp4/ship-3 commit with c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic baked as the image's serving default
# (ENV QWEN_C2_PROFILE) and THATCH_SERVING_SESSION_CAP baked as its max-num-seqs (8): the profile, its owner traffic waiver (id w2-er-fx-262k-2026-10-11, decision APPROVED,
# committed) and the bake are the ship pack's. The image is the ship image plus ONE correctness fix and nothing else on top of the ship image: the API server swaps the
# argument converter of vLLM 0.25.1's qwen3 tool-call parser (it strip()s every <parameter=...> value, so a written file loses its final newline and an edit loses its
# indentation) for the exact inverse of the chat template, which removes the one framing newline at each end and nothing else (scripts/ci/c2_toolcall_whitespace.py; ON for
# every profile; QWEN_C2_TOOLCALL_WS=0 turns it off). No device code, no profile env and no token the model generates changes. HOW THE FIX REACHES THE IMAGE:
# docker/qwen-c2-overlay.txt, the ONE image list (generated from scripts/ci/fusion-wp/TW.json), names c2_toolcall_whitespace.py, toolcall_whitespace_smoke.py and
# test_c2_toolcall_whitespace.py beside serving_c2_contract.py (which arms the fix in boot() and is overlaid already); the build's in-image test run executes
# test_c2_toolcall_whitespace against the image's installed vLLM (its EngineTests class runs the real parsers). The CPU suite must be green on the tagged commit (gh
# workflow run qwen-cpu-suite.yml -f ref=<sha>) and the tag is pushed on THAT commit. READ: 'baking the serving default
# c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic with a session cap of 8', the provenance report '(c) the image default is the BAKED profile ...', no problem
# line, the in-image unit test run ending OK, the image id. Estimate 35 minutes (the tp4-ship-1 build took 35).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-ship-3
C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic
